CR30 protocol slice — vendored third-party code
================================================

The Python modules in this directory (packets.py, device.py, protocol.py) are
a trimmed copy of the `cr30reader` package from:

    itohio/color-science  —  https://github.com/itohio/color-science
    License: MIT (see LICENSE-itohio in this directory)

Reverse-engineering writeup:
    https://itohi.com/colorimetry/reverse-engineering-cr30/

Only the low-level serial protocol needed to (a) connect, (b) run black/white
calibration, and (c) read the raw 31-band spectral power distribution (SPD) has
been kept. The upstream colour-science, Argyll, GUI, CLI and driver layers were
intentionally dropped — epaper-colorcal does its own colorimetry with the
`colour-science` package.

Local modifications:
  - Removed the unused `import numpy as np` from protocol.py.
  - No functional changes to the protocol/packet logic.

Keeping this as a clean, attributed copy (rather than a dependency) so the
reverse-engineered protocol can be patched for specific CR30 units/firmware.
